/P 17 0 R
/E (Highly informative tourist sites aim to educate visitors through signage and exhibits, yet tourists often prioritize movement, visual attractions, and photography over engaging with informational content. This creates a gap between the intended educational value of these spaces and the way visitors actually experience them. The challenge is to enhance information consumption without disrupting natural visitor behaviour.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [181]
>>
